rson  i have to go out sometimes but that's a  training thing that definitely is  ongoing um i've been leash training her  and she's doing so well she was really  bad puller at the start and i would say  she's still not walking like right next  to me which is supposed to be the ideal  but she's pretty damn close she just  loves sniffing so she'll always walk  around and just sniff a bunch of stuff  but she um she's gotten so much better  on the leash so so so far she's just  really quick to train it's kind of what  i'm saying she's a beautiful dog she's a  big beautiful dog  i mostly have largely like very positive  things to say about her essentially um  yeah some minor behavioral issues  obviously medical issue but none of it  is for her she's a beautiful dog i just  wanted to be in a house with like a lot  of people or a family or other dogs just  so that she has company and she can  start to feel more confident and more at  home and like like one person isn't her  sole responsibility um so that that  anxiety gets a little bit more  manageable and yeah thank you for  watching if you would like to adopt  queen bee check out the link in the  description she's from pasadena humane  and i'm gonna continue to foster dogs is  the plan so i will foster another dog  and i will like kind of learn their  behaviors and let you guys know who they  are and who i think they would fit for  and this beautiful girl just needs a lot  of love somebody will give her a lot of  love and a lot of cuddles clearly she's  very content with cuddles  very large lap dog but  i wouldn't have it any other way thank  you for watching good luck to my sweet  baby queen bee as they call her finding  a home  you're gonna be great everybody loves  you  you're gonna be great oh thank you
 

